# KAMEN FIGHT — RIDER LEVEL TRAINER EVALUATION REPORT

**Target Candidate Model:** `002_001` (Kamen Rider Nigo)

**Architecture:** `v5-state256-action17` | **Patch:** `charge1-reset1`

**Verification Status:** **PASSED** (All 4 difficulty tiers achieved >50% Win Rate)

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Verification Target

The newly trained candidate model `002_001` (Nigo) was subjected to benchmark evaluations under the **RIDER difficulty engine**, which enforces search-selected charge preservation and directional charge-clock reset mechanics.

The candidate successfully passed the validation threshold across **all four difficulty tiers**, maintaining a **>50% win rate** against every opponent controller:

* **SOUL AI (Deep MCTS Search):** **52.0% Win Rate** (13W / 12L)
* **MASTER AI (High MCTS Search):** **73.7% Win Rate** (14W / 5L)
* **BALANCED AI (Mid MCTS / Heuristic):** **61.8% Win Rate** (21W / 13L)
* **EASY AI (Direct Network Policy):** **58.8% Win Rate** (10W / 7L)

---

## 2. Comparative Performance Matrix Across Difficulty Tiers

| Metric | SOUL AI | MASTER AI | BALANCED AI | EASY AI |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Evaluated Policy** | `rider` (Search) | `rider` (Search) | `rider` (Search) | `network` (Direct) |
| **Win Rate (W / L)** | **52.0%** (13 / 12) | **73.7%** (14 / 5) | **61.8%** (21 / 13) | **58.8%** (10 / 7) |
| **Avg. Rounds / Match** | 13.6 | 13.9 | 13.4 | **24.0** |
| **Mean Selected Q** | 0.9434 | 0.9522 | 0.9459 | **1.7844** |
| **W-Stance (Utility)** | 4.9% (17) | 8.7% (23) | 4.8% (22) | **38.8% (159)** |
| **A-Stance (Defense)** | 3.2% (11) | 1.9% (5) | 2.6% (12) | 2.9% (12) |
| **S-Stance (Special)** | 41.3% (142) | 46.0% (122) | 42.3% (192) | 23.9% (98) |
| **D-Stance (Physical)** | 44.2% (152) | 38.5% (102) | 45.6% (207) | 32.2% (132) |
| **IDLE (Forced Stun)** | 6.4% (22) | 4.9% (13) | 4.6% (21) | 2.2% (9) |

---

## 3. Strategic Adaptation Analysis

Candidate Nigo (`002`) dynamically alters its operational profile based on opponent difficulty, search depth, and execution risk:

### A. Vs. High-Search Opponents (Master 73.7% & Soul 52.0%)

* **Ground Brawling Shift:** Nigo abandons lengthy setup sequences and suppresses non-damaging utility (W-stance usage stays under 9%). Against deep MCTS search trees, spending turns on zero-damage buffs invites unmitigated counter-attacks.
* **The `D+I` $\rightarrow$ `S+J` / `S+L` Resource Engine:** Nigo relies on **D+I Mixed Combo** (1 Chi cost, 130 Dmg, 82% Hit, net +1 Chi refund) to continuously build Chi and faint pressure. When Chi thresholds are met, Nigo converts into **S+J Rider Punch** (3 Chi, 370 Dmg) for fast dumps or **S+L Rider Power Kick** (7 Chi, 860 Dmg) for heavy punishments.
* **Charge Clock Optimization:** Under the `rider` policy, Nigo maintains **85%–100% charge levels** on decisive turns. High charge ensures priority during simultaneous execution ties.

### B. Vs. Mid-Search Opponents (Balanced 61.8%)

* **Balanced Damage Profile:** Nigo establishes a 45.6% Physical (`D`) and 42.3% Special (`S`) distribution.
* **P1/P2 Neutrality:** Nigo shows balanced performance regardless of starting side (P1: 11W–6L vs P2: 10W–7L), leveraging **W+I Rider Power Jump** (20 uses) to gain +20 Accuracy and 1.35x Attack multiplier to override starting frame discrepancies.

### C. Vs. Low-Search / Direct Net Opponents (Easy 58.8%)

* **Utility & Buff Farming (38.8% W-Stance):** When facing an unguided direct network policy, Nigo shifts to a cautious, utility-heavy posture, casting **W+I Rider Power Jump** 130 times (31.7% of all actions) and **W+K Power Focus** 26 times.
* **Marathon Attrition:** Without deep MCTS threat pressure, Nigo safe-farms Chi reserves up to 16 Chi, elongating match length to **24.0 average rounds** (e.g., Match #5 running 41 rounds) to secure near-zero risk victories.

---

## 4. Key Demo Match Sequence Breakdown

Below is a detailed tactical breakdown of representative winning games from each evaluation run:

### Game 1: Vs. Soul AI (Match #6, 12 Rounds) — Stun-Lock Exploitation

* **Rounds 1–4:** Nigo opens with **S+L @ 100%** (860 Dmg), followed by **D+I** pokes, chunking Soul Nigo down to 942 LP while inflicting heavy Faint damage.
* **Round 5 Punish:** On Round 4, Soul Nigo hits **100 Fnt lockout**. On Round 5, Nigo capitalizes on Soul's forced `DO_NOTHING @ 0%` by dropping an unpunished **S+K Rider Flying Knee @ 90%** (480 Dmg).
* **Rounds 10–12 Finish:** After recovering from a mid-game faint on Round 11, Nigo executes **S+J Rider Punch @ 100%** on Round 12 for the KO.

### Game 2: Vs. Master AI (Match #1, 15 Rounds) — Precision Buff Integration

* **Rounds 1–6:** Nigo opens with **S+L @ 90%** and **S+K** volleys, forcing Master Nigo into a Round 5 Faint lockout. Nigo punishes Round 6 with **S+K @ 100%** (bringing Master down to 1,192 LP).
* **Rounds 8–9 Buff Setup:** Nigo weaves **W+I Rider Power Jump** (Round 8) and **W+K Power Focus** (Round 9, 2.5x `dAttack` multiplier) into neutral play while Master guards.
* **Round 15 Finisher:** Fully buffed and with 0 Chi remaining on Master, Nigo fires a **100% S+L Rider Power Kick** to close the match.

### Game 3: Vs. Master AI (Match #5, 11 Rounds) — Turn 11 `S+I` Nuke

* **Rounds 1–3:** Nigo stacks back-to-back **S+L** and **S+J** strikes, eroding Master's LP to 2,052 while holding a full health bar (2,640 LP).
* **Rounds 9–10 Control:** Nigo casts **W+I Power Jump @ 100%** on Round 9, followed by **D+J** on Round 10 to push Master Nigo to **100 Fnt**.
* **Round 11 Nuke:** With Master immobilized in `DO_NOTHING @ 0%`, Nigo unleashes **S+I Typhoon Power Break @ 100%** (10 Chi, 1,065 Base Damage), vaporizing Master's remaining LP instantly!

### Game 4: Vs. Balanced AI (Match #1, 9 Rounds) — Turn 2 `S+I` Opening

* **Round 1–2 Nuke:** Nigo absorbs an opening trade on Round 1, then immediately fires **S+I Typhoon Power Break @ 100%** on Round 2, dropping Balanced Nigo from 3,300 to 1,925 LP on turn two.
* **Rounds 6–9 Execution:** Nigo uses **W+I Jump** on Round 5 for airborne accuracy, lands **S+L @ 99%** on Round 6 (reducing opponent to 434 LP), and finishes with back-to-back **S+J Rider Punches**.

### Game 5: Vs. Easy AI (Match #5, 41 Rounds) — The 41-Round Marathon

* **Rounds 1–20:** Nigo repeatedly uses **W+I Power Jump** to maintain airborne evasion while building a max-capped bank of 16 Chi.
* **Rounds 21–41:** Nigo systematically chips away at Easy Nigo's health with low-risk **D+J** and **D+K** pokes, finishing the game on Round 41 with **S+J Rider Punch** while maintaining 565 LP.

---

## 5. Technical Validation & Engine Compatibility

1. **Charging Schema Alignment:** The candidate model strictly adhered to `v5-state256-action17` / `charge1-reset1`. No invalid charge clock state overflows were detected across all 1,473 recorded round decisions.
2. **Q-Value Stabilization:** Mean selected Q-values remained highly consistent across MCTS search difficulties (Soul: `0.9434`, Master: `0.9522`, Balanced: `0.9459`), demonstrating well-calibrated value functions.
3. **Search Charge Preservation:** The `rider` evaluation policy successfully preserved search-selected charge values, eliminating priority loss bugs present in earlier build iterations.

---

## 6. Final Recommendation

The candidate model `002_001` (Nigo) has met all strategic performance benchmarks and exceeded the mandatory **>50% win rate threshold** across all RIDER difficulty levels.

**Recommended Next Actions:**

1. Execute **`ACTIVATE SELECTED CANDIDATE`** to promote `002_001` to the Active slot.
2. Perform **`EXPORT SELECTED CANDIDATE`** immediately to prevent RAM loss following persistent storage save warnings.







