# KAMEN FIGHT — RIDER LEVEL TRAINER EVALUATION REPORT

**Target Candidate Model:** `001_003`

**Learner:** Kamen Rider Ichigo (`001`)

**Opponent:** Kamen Rider V3 (`003`)

**Architecture:** `v5-state256-action17` | **Patch:** `charge1-reset1`

**Evaluation Policy:** `rider` (Live MCTS Search)

**Verification Status:** **PASSED** (All 4 difficulty tiers achieved >50% Win Rate)

---

## 1. Executive Summary

Candidate model `001_003` (Kamen Rider Ichigo trained to fight Kamen Rider V3) was evaluated across all four standard difficulty tiers under the RIDER engine.

Ichigo successfully passed the validation benchmark across **all four difficulty pools**, maintaining a dominant win rate over V3’s search tree policies:

* **SOUL AI (Deep MCTS Search):** **68.4% Win Rate** (26W / 12L)
* **MASTER AI (High MCTS Search):** **56.0% Win Rate** (14W / 11L)
* **BALANCED AI (Mid MCTS / Heuristic):** **75.0% Win Rate** (24W / 8L)
* **EASY AI (Direct Network Policy):** **75.9% Win Rate** (41W / 13L)

---

## 2. Benchmark Performance Matrix Across Tiers

| Metric | SOUL AI | MASTER AI | BALANCED AI | EASY AI |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Learner / Opponent** | **Ichigo / V3** | **Ichigo / V3** | **Ichigo / V3** | **Ichigo / V3** |
| **Win Rate (W / L)** | **68.4%** (26 / 12) | **56.0%** (14 / 11) | **75.0%** (24 / 8) | **75.9%** (41 / 13) |
| **P1 Slot Win Rate** | 73.7% (14W / 5L) | 46.2% (6W / 7L) | 68.8% (11W / 5L) | 66.7% (18W / 9L) |
| **P2 Slot Win Rate** | **63.2%** (12W / 7L) | **66.7%** (8W / 4L) | **81.3%** (13W / 3L) | **85.2%** (23W / 4L) |
| **Avg. Rounds / Match** | 13.4 | 13.8 | 14.0 | 13.3 |
| **Mean Selected Q** | 1.3714 | 1.3550 | 1.3828 | 1.4133 |
| **W-Stance (Utility)** | 3.3% (17) | 6.1% (21) | 3.3% (15) | 5.0% (36) |
| **A-Stance (Defense)** | 2.0% (10) | 0.9% (3) | 2.9% (13) | 2.2% (16) |
| **S-Stance (Special)** | **47.0% (239)** | **41.7% (144)** | **44.4% (200)** | **47.3% (339)** |
| **D-Stance (Physical)** | **39.0% (198)** | **43.5% (150)** | **42.9% (193)** | **38.5% (276)** |
| **IDLE (Forced Stun)** | 8.7% (44) | 7.8% (27) | 6.4% (29) | 6.8% (49) |

---

## 3. Strategic Adaptation: How Ichigo Countered V3

Ichigo’s neural controller adapted its tactical profile specifically to exploit structural weaknesses in V3’s moveset and AI search behavior:

```
                      Ichigo Counter-Strategy vs. V3
                      
   [ Early S+L Rider Kick ] ──► Chunk V3 LP to <2,100 ──► [ Punish V3 W+L Casts ]
   (860 Base Dmg, 100% Chg)                                (Intercept Startup)
              │                                                    │
              ▼                                                    ▼
   [ D-Pokes & S+J Punch ] ──►  [ Trigger 100 Fnt Lockout ] ──► [ S+L / S+I Finisher ]
   (Build Chi & Faint Meter)     (Target Immobilized)          (Guaranteed KO)

```

### A. Exploiting V3's `W+L` (Double Typhoon) Recovery Blunders

* V3 frequently relies on **`W+L` Double Typhoon** to clear faint or generate buffs mid-fight.
* Ichigo's policy learned to aggressively punish these zero/low-damage startup frames with **`S+L` Rider Power Kick** (860 Base Dmg) or **`S+J` Rider Punch** (370 Base Dmg), turning V3's utility turns into immediate health deficits for V3.

### B. High Special Efficiency (`S+L` & `S+J` Dual Engine)

Across all jobs, Ichigo spent **41.7% to 47.3%** of its choices in `S`-stance:

* **`S+L` Rider Power Kick (Heavy Finisher):** Accounted for **34% to 49%** of all Special moves (e.g., 119 uses vs SOUL, 153 uses vs EASY). Used as a high-charge opener and stun-punish.
* **`S+J` Rider Punch (Burst Valve):** Used as a rapid 3-Chi dump (74 uses vs SOUL, 126 uses vs EASY) to maintain pressure without stalling for 7–10 Chi.

### C. Superior Performance in P2 Position

Unlike earlier iterations that struggled when starting second, Candidate Ichigo achieved exceptional win rates in the P2 slot:

* **85.2% P2 Win Rate vs Easy AI** (23W / 4L)
* **81.3% P2 Win Rate vs Balanced AI** (13W / 3L)
* **66.7% P2 Win Rate vs Master AI** (8W / 4L)
Ichigo leverages high-charge **`S+L`** and **`W+I` Power Jump** positioning to negate P1's initial frame advantage.

---

## 4. Key Demo Match Sequence Breakdown

### Game #1: Vs. SOUL AI (Match #1, 10 Rounds) — Turn 10 Stun Execution

* **Rounds 1–3:** Ichigo opens Round 1 with **`S+L` @ 90%**, dealing heavy damage and leaving V3 at 2,103 LP. Ichigo follows up with **`D+L`** and **`S+J`** to rapidly push V3’s faint bar.
* **Rounds 5–6:** V3 attempts to cast **`W+L` Double Typhoon** twice (Rounds 5 & 6). Ichigo punishes with **`S+J`** and **`D+L`**, bringing V3 to 1,451 LP.
* **Rounds 9–10:** Ichigo casts **`W+I` Power Jump @ 100%** on Round 9 while V3 guards in `A+I`. On Round 10, with V3 stunned in `DO_NOTHING @ 0%`, Ichigo executes a **100% `S+L` Rider Power Kick** for an absolute KO with 1,738 LP remaining!

### Game #2: Vs. MASTER AI (Match #1, 11 Rounds) — 2,182 LP Flawless Victory

* **Rounds 1–3:** Ichigo opens with **`S+L` @ 100%** on Round 1, dropping V3 to 2,075 LP on turn one. Follows with **`D+L`** and **`S+K`** on Round 3 to bring V3 to 1,477 LP.
* **Rounds 9–11:** Ichigo connects back-to-back **`D+K`** pokes on Rounds 9 & 10, driving V3 directly into a **100 Fnt lockout**. On Round 11, Ichigo delivers a **100% `S+L` Rider Power Kick** to finish V3 cleanly.

### Game #3: Vs. BALANCED AI (Match #3, 13 Rounds) — Triple `S+L` Bombardment

* **Rounds 1–4:** Ichigo stacks **`S+L` @ 100%** on Round 1, **`D+L`** on Round 2, and another **`S+L` @ 100%** on Round 3, reducing V3 from 3,000 down to 1,118 LP by Round 4.
* **Rounds 8–13:** After a mid-game faint recovery, Ichigo lands **`S+K`** on Round 9 (pushing V3 to 358 LP) and finishes the fight on Round 13 with **`S+J` Rider Punch**.

### Game #4: Vs. EASY AI (Match #5, 14 Rounds) — 2,052 LP Domination

* **Rounds 1–8:** Ichigo connects three separate **`S+L` Rider Power Kicks** (Rounds 1, 4, and 7/8), leaving V3 clinging to just 48 LP while Ichigo retains 2,207 LP.
* **Rounds 11–14:** Ichigo uses **`A+L` Guard** on Round 11 and **`W+I` Power Jump** on Round 12 to neutralize V3's remaining Chi, sealing the match on Round 14 with **`S+J` Rider Punch**.

